The previous issues were caused by `syncActiveIndexToValue` resetting the temporary active cursor position back to the currently committed selection (or the first option) when public properties (`options` or `value`) were updated, or by not properly syncing internal state variables in response to reactive updates. 

Under test conditions, changing the selection or options might dynamically trigger reactivity updates which reset `this.activeIndex`. To ensure robust state handling where the cursor position is correctly maintained and correctly dispatched, we have separated the tracking of the active descendant index from the public selection flow.

Here is the complete, corrected code.

File: force-app/main/default/lwc/statusListbox/statusListbox.js
